plain literals
1.5           Double   1.5
123.456       Double   123.456
0.0           Double   0

suffixes, in either case
123.456s      Single   123.456
123.456S      Single   123.456
123.456d      Double   123.456
19.99m        Decimal  19.99
100m          Decimal  100

exponents
1.5e3         Double   1500
1.5E-3        Double   0.0015
2.5e10s       Single   2.5E+10
(a decimal literal takes no exponent)

digits group with _ wherever they fall
1_000.000_1   Double   1000.0001
1_2_3.4_5     Double   123.45

there is no hexadecimal floating-point literal, and
no implicit conversion, so a mixed expression is a
compile error until one side is cast
1.0 + cast(1) Double   2
